 "name": "blueprint-ranked-2026-06",
 "notes": "Source: https://blueprintcoc.com/blogs/town-hall-16/best-th16-trophy-base (\"Best TH16 Ranked Mode/Trophy Base of 2026 with Link\"), published 2026-06-22, article by Loki, base credited to the Blueprint CoC builder team (no individual builder named). Layout link: https://link.clashofclans.com/en/?action=OpenLayout&id=TH16%3AHV%3AAAAAQgAAAAJUMcThgSfkw1SX7Qoe6MuZ . Images: https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0472/7265/7051/files/TH16_ranked.jpg (village view, 2880x1620) and .../th16_trap_view.jpg (trap view). Article: tested vs RC-walk Root Riders, Clone Hydra, Super Archer spam, Bat Witches; recommended CC 1 Lava Hound + 1 Furnace + 3 Archers (not applied: cc_troops left at the project default).\nDigitized 2026-10-21 with tools/baselab/digitize.py. Grid fitted to the cyan building-pad outlines (cx 1361.7, top -138.4, a 29.118, b 21.822; median pad-corner residual 0.02 tile). Walls: automatic pale-cap detection (lift 20 px) minus building footprints, plus 6 isolated wall posts and 4 gap fills read by eye ((12,15),(6,28),(36,30),(36,31)); 265 walls found. The image cuts off the bottom village corner (tiles with x+y >= ~80) and tall buildings hide some walls, so up to 60 walls are not recorded (325 at TH16). All 98 buildings hand-transcribed (key x y), positions checked against pad outlines and zoomed overlays; building identities checked against Clash of Clans wiki images.\nKnown uncertainties: (1) dd 40 40 is IMPUTED (3rd Dark Elixir Drill not visible; placed in the cut-off corner). gm 37 40 is only partly visible. (2) The 5 Hidden Teslas are only visible in the trap view: 13 4, 16 4, 19 4 (top rage section, just inside the y=3 wall) and 14 36, 16 37 (bottom-left rage section); each +-1 tile. (3) Positions read from graphics without a visible pad edge (eagle, hero hall, workshop, banners, sweepers, bh 26 16 / 26 26 / 16 25, xbows 28 12 / 10 11, ad 32 10, at 27 0) are +-1 tile. (4) Modes are assumptions: infernos single (single/multi not distinguishable at this resolution; the article mentions 'both Inferno Towers' in the core), x-bows both, spell towers rage (article: 'two Rage Spell Tower sections'), sweepers facing NW (24 15) and SW (24 25) toward the rage sections per the article. No Crafting Station visible (optional, seasonal). Levels not set (engine defaults).\nTraps: NOT transcribed. The trap view shows them but they are stacked too densely to read tile by tile. Trap clusters seen in the trap view (main-image tile coordinates): top rage section around x 12-22, y 3-11 (giant bombs, springs, small bombs, skeleton traps, seeking air mines, tornado per the article); a red air-bomb 'farm' around x 13-18, y 26-31 (away from the TH, per the article: 'Warden ability trap'); bottom-left rage section around x 13-22, y 32-40. Leave trap placement to the trap-placement step, constrained to these clusters.",
